# proxy.Dockerfile.dockerignore
#
# proxy.Dockerfile's build context is the repo root ("."), but the build
# itself clones KataProxy fresh from GitHub (see proxy.Dockerfile) and
# needs no local files at all. This keeps the context Docker sends to the
# daemon small instead of shipping the whole monorepo (frontend/
# node_modules-adjacent source, backend/, docs/, git history) for a build
# that reads none of it. BuildKit picks this up automatically for the
# Dockerfile of the same basename (proxy.Dockerfile) in preference to a
# root .dockerignore, which this repo does not otherwise have.
*
